Statement of Purpose

The laws of most jurisdictions throughout the world automatically confer exclusive Copyright and Related Rights upon the creator and subsequent owner(s). Certain owners wish to permanently relinquish those rights for the benefit of the public.

Waiver

To the greatest extent permitted by, but not in contravention of, applicable law, the Affirmer waives, abandons, and surrenders all Copyright and Related Rights and associated claims and causes of action in the Work, whether now known or unknown.

Public License Fallback

Should any part of the waiver be judged legally invalid or ineffective, the Affirmer grants every affected person a royalty-free, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, non-exclusive, irrevocable and unconditional license to exercise the waived rights for any purpose.

Limitations and Disclaimers

The Work is provided as-is and without warranties. This notice does not affect patent, trademark, privacy or publicity rights, and it does not relicense third-party material.

